&Q000469

{1 = 1-8}
9=1.	For @wDN{Enlil}, whose statements are powerful, the profoundly far-sighted knowledgeable judge, 
13=2.	who issues decisions, whose utterances are immutable, who places the …… in his hands -- @wRN{Išme-@wDN{Dagan}}, 
17=3.	the mighty man with muscles and body of a lion, the strong awe-inspiring youth who alone is august, 
21=4.	the lord whose sweet name is invoked in all the lands, 
25=5.	under whose rule the living creatures multiply, makes the black-headed people, 
29=6.	its settled people who were entrusted to him for protection, 
33=7.	proceed with the firstling-offerings of the land. 
37=8.	He does not …… in his good palace. 

{9 = 9-22}
41=9.	Then @wRN{Išme-@wDN{Dagan}} the youthful, the mightiest hero among swift athletes, the fearsome runner, 
45=10.	who serving night and day never ceases caring for @wSN{Nibru} -- the city where the seed of the numerous people came forth and where life and birth came into existence -- and who provides daily for everything, 
49=11.	established justice (?) on a grand scale. 
53=12.	The king whose rising is a hurricane, 
57=13.	a flood, 
61=14.	a wind blowing in its fury, 
65=15.	who swinging his wide open arms flashes away into the distance, 
69=16.	who is like a fierce lion of the desert which advances in full strength and vigour, 
73=17.	who runs fast on the roadway …… battle and combat, 
77=18.	a horse waving its tail on the highway, 
81=19.	who like a young deer …… running, 
85=20.	…… knees are swift and indefatigable, 
89=21.	the son who provides @wDN{Enlil} with everything, 
93=22.	who causes joy to @wDN{Ninlil's} heart -- he will never stop caring for the shining shrine. 

{23 = 23-28}
97=23.	Then @wRN{Išme-@wDN{Dagan}} erected a statue on his precious dais in the @wTN{E-ni-guru}, 
101=24.	depicting him as inspiring terror while running in a storm, 
105=25.	and made it iridescent with splendour, 
109=26.	so that the great prince of the entire heaven, 
113=27.	the lord whose utterance is immutable, 
117=28.	should constantly direct his shining forehead and favourable glance at the true shepherd whom he engendered. 

{29 = 29-35}
121=29.	If a king issues evil orders concerning this statue, 
125=30.	and erases its inscription and writes his own name on it; 
129=31.	or, because of this curse, he makes another man raise his hand against it, 
133=32.	then may @wDN{Enlil} my lord and @wDN{Ninlil} my lady curse that man! 
137=33.	May @wDN{Enki}, @wDN{Iškur}, @wDN{Ezina}, @wDN{Šakkan}, 
141=34.	the lords of abundance, 
35.	…… him cruelly by withholding abundance from heaven and earth under his rule! 
